clang: the EmiBSD driver links with the system's link defaults

Why a patch: the system's libraries are linked with two lld options the
inherited build expects of the system's own linker: --undefined-version (a
version script may name a symbol the library does not define; libc's
Symbols.list names __data_start) and --ignore-function-address-equality (a
function's address need not be unique, so protected symbols stay
preemptible). Upstream lld turns neither on by default, and the userland
gave both to every link through a clang configuration file of its own. This
makes the EmiBSD driver pass them on every link it makes, before the user's
arguments, so -Wl,--no-undefined-version still turns the first off. In the
driver, not in lld: a direct ld.lld invocation (the kernel's) is unchanged.
Applies over 0003, which creates ToolChains/EmiBSD.cpp. Written by EmiBSD
(ISC); carried by DevTools over the pinned tag. Author: Emilio Navarrete
Lineros, 2026-11-08.

--- a/clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/EmiBSD.cpp
+++ b/clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/EmiBSD.cpp
@@ -70,6 +70,14 @@
 
   // The unwinder finds the frames through the eh_frame header.
   CmdArgs.push_back("--eh-frame-hdr");
+
+  // What the system's libraries are linked with: a version script may name a
+  // symbol the library does not define (libc's Symbols.list names
+  // __data_start), and a function's address need not be unique, so protected
+  // symbols stay preemptible. Before the user's arguments, so that
+  // -Wl,--no-undefined-version still turns the first off.
+  CmdArgs.push_back("--undefined-version");
+  CmdArgs.push_back("--ignore-function-address-equality");
   if (Static) {
     CmdArgs.push_back("-Bstatic");
   } else {
